<cem:description lang="en">This virtual learning object "WRITING SPOT Writing a Paragraph about Personal Experiences" that makes part of the lesson No: 10, Reminiscing With Friends, which in turn belongs to the Upper-intermediate (B2.3) of the teaching of English as a Foreign Language, is intended to work on: tell stories and anecdotes; express emotions and feelings. The grammar of this LO refers to: perfect modals to talk about uncertainty past events, e.g., i can't have been there more than a couple months before i was promoted to head chef; review all past tenses: past continuous, simple past, and present perfect, e.g., i spent the next couple months weeding out incompetent waitstaff, developing guideline for food preparation, working with new suppliers. Also, the vocabulary considers: relationships and character traits, e.g. relationships, responsible, etc; beliefs and opinions, e.g. chaos, strengths, weaknesses, etc.</cem:description>
</cem:resource>
